WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.350
Step into many Jewish kitchens
and you may find two sinks.

2
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.910
Two sets of plates, pans and
cutlery, often colour-coded.

3
00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:10.900
Some animals may be eaten.

4
00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:13.600
Others, such as the pig, never.

5
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:17.620
And packaged food often carries
a small supervision mark.

6
00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:22.240
So why would a kitchen need two sinks,
and what makes food kosher in the first

7
00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:23.250
place?

8
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:28.290
In this mission, you'll read the Torah's
own tests for which animals may be eaten.

9
00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:31.810
Then you'll weigh up the reasons
Jews give for keeping these laws,

10
00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:34.370
from holiness to self-discipline.

11
00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:37.550
Your mission: find out
what makes food kosher,

12
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.120
and why a kitchen might need two sinks.
